---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const updated = '4 April 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Lili David"
  description="How CoherentOrgs SRL collects, uses, and protects your personal data on lilidavid.com."
>

  <section class="page-hero section privacy-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="label">Legal</span>
      <h1 class="mt-sm">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="lead mt-md privacy-intro">
        Your privacy matters. This page explains what personal data is collected when you
        use this website, why it is collected, and what rights you have over it.
      </p>
      <p class="privacy-updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section privacy-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="privacy-body">

        <div class="privacy-block">
          <h2>Who is responsible for your data</h2>
          <p>
            This website is operated by <strong>CoherentOrgs SRL</strong>, the legal entity
            behind the work of Lili David. CoherentOrgs SRL is the data controller for all
            personal data collected through this website.
          </p>
          <address class="privacy-address">
            CoherentOrgs SRL<br />
            Str Ion Lahovari 23B/2, Dumbraveni, Romania<br />
            Registration Number: RO54128042<br />
            Contact: <a href="mailto:connect@lilidavid.com">connect@lilidavid.com</a>
          </address>
        </div>

        <div class="privacy-block">
          <h2>What data is collected and why</h2>

          <h3>Contact form</h3>
          <p>
            When you submit the contact form on this website, the following information is
            collected: your name, email address, organisation (optional), and your message.
          </p>
          <p>
            This data is collected solely to respond to your enquiry. It is not used for
            marketing, shared with third parties for commercial purposes, or added to any
            mailing list.
          </p>
          <p>
            The legal basis for this processing is <strong>Legitimate Interest</strong>
            (Article&nbsp;6(1)(f) GDPR): when you reach out through a professional enquiry form,
            it is mutually expected that the information you provide will be used to respond to you.
          </p>

          <h3>Booking a call</h3>
          <p>
            This website embeds a scheduling widget from <strong>TidyCal</strong> (tidycal.com) so you
            can book an introductory call without leaving the site. If you choose to book a call,
            your booking details are collected by TidyCal, where TidyCal acts as an independent data
            controller. Your booking data is subject to <a
              href="https://tidycal.com/privacy"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              aria-label="TidyCal privacy policy (opens in a new tab)"
            >TidyCal's
            own Privacy Policy</a>, not this one.
          </p>

          <h3>No analytics or tracking</h3>
          <p>
            This website does not use Google Analytics, Facebook Pixel, or any other behavioural
            tracking or advertising technology. No tracking cookies are placed on your device
            by this website.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="privacy-block">
          <h2>How your data is handled</h2>

          <h3>Form submission service</h3>
          <p>
            Contact form submissions are processed by <strong>FormSubmit</strong>
            (formsubmit.co), which forwards your message to Lili's email inbox.
            FormSubmit is a US-based service. When you use the contact form, your
            data will be transferred to servers outside the European Economic Area.
            FormSubmit does not currently publish a formal Data Processing Agreement
            or EU-approved transfer safeguards.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you would prefer not to use the form, you are welcome to email
            <a href="mailto:connect@lilidavid.com">connect@lilidavid.com</a> directly.
            Emails sent directly do not pass through FormSubmit.
          </p>

          <h3>Email inbox</h3>
          <p>
            Once forwarded by FormSubmit, your message is received and stored in
            Lili's email inbox. Enquiry emails are retained for up to two years and
            then deleted, unless an ongoing working relationship requires longer retention.
          </p>

          <h3>Fonts</h3>
          <p>
            The fonts used on this website (Inter and Playfair Display) are served
            directly from this website's own servers. No font files are loaded from
            Google Fonts or any other external CDN, so no data is sent to third parties
            as a result of viewing this site.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="privacy-block">
          <h2>Cookies</h2>
          <p>
            This website does not place any cookies on your device for tracking or
            analytics purposes. The contact form uses a honeypot field (an invisible
            field to detect spam bots) but this does not involve cookies or tracking.
          </p>
          <p>
            If the optional spam-protection widget (Cloudflare Turnstile) is enabled
            on the contact form, Cloudflare may set a cookie as part of its bot-detection
            process. This cookie is functional in nature and does not track you across
            other websites.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="privacy-block">
          <h2>Your rights</h2>
          <p>
            Under the GDPR, you have the following rights in relation to your personal data:
          </p>
          <ul class="privacy-rights">
            <li><strong>Right of access</strong> — You can request a copy of the personal data held about you.</li>
            <li><strong>Right to rectification</strong> — You can ask for inaccurate data to be corrected.</li>
            <li><strong>Right to erasure</strong> — You can ask for your data to be deleted, where there is no overriding reason to keep it.</li>
            <li><strong>Right to restriction</strong> — You can ask for processing of your data to be restricted in certain circumstances.</li>
            <li><strong>Right to data portability</strong> — You can ask to receive your data in a structured, machine-readable format.</li>
            <li><strong>Right to object</strong> — You can object to processing based on legitimate interest. Processing will stop unless there are compelling legitimate grounds that override your interests.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            To exercise any of these rights, please email
            <a href="mailto:connect@lilidavid.com">connect@lilidavid.com</a>.
            Requests will be responded to within 30 days.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="privacy-block">
          <h2>Right to complain</h2>
          <p>
            If you believe your data has been handled unlawfully, you have the right to
            lodge a complaint with the Romanian data protection supervisory authority:
          </p>
          <address class="privacy-address">
            Autoritatea Națională de Supraveghere a Prelucrării Datelor cu Caracter Personal
            (ANSPDCP)<br />
            <a
              href="https://www.dataprotection.ro"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              aria-label="ANSPDCP website (opens in a new tab)"
            >www.dataprotection.ro</a>
          </address>
          <p>
            You also have the right to bring a complaint before the supervisory authority in
            the EU member state where you live or work.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="privacy-block">
          <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p>
            This policy may be updated from time to time. The date at the top of this page
            reflects when it was last revised. Significant changes will be noted here.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="privacy-block">
          <h2>See also</h2>
          <p>
            <a href="/accessibility">Accessibility</a>
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>

<style>
  .privacy-hero {
    padding-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .privacy-intro {
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  .privacy-updated {
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .privacy-section.section {
    padding-top: var(--space-md);
  }

  .privacy-body {
    max-width: 70ch;
  }

  .privacy-block {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--stone-dark);
  }

  .privacy-block:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
    margin-bottom: 0;
    padding-bottom: 0;
  }

  .privacy-block h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 2.5vw, 1.75rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    line-height: 1.25;
  }

  .privacy-block h3 {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
  }

  .privacy-block p {
    max-width: none;
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
  }

  .privacy-block p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .privacy-block a {
    color: #3F5648;
    text-underline-offset: 0.18em;
  }

  .privacy-block a:hover {
    color: var(--eucalyptus);
  }

  .privacy-address {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    font-style: normal;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    padding-left: var(--space-sm);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--stone-dark);
  }

  .privacy-rights {
    margin: var(--space-sm) 0;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.6rem;
  }

  .privacy-rights li {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .privacy-rights li strong {
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
